# Porsche Cayenne 9PA four-door 4x4, 2003-2010.
#
# Porsche's first 4x4, developed with Volkswagen: 4,782 mm long, 1,928 mm wide,
# 1,699 mm high, 2,855 mm wheelbase; 3.2 V6 and 4.5 V8, permanent four-wheel
# drive. Facelift in 2007. A controversial but commercially successful luxury
# 4x4 in Britain. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porsche_Cayenne
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Grey and Dark Blue are documented Porsche colours of
# the period.
#
# Weight: 30 in total (black 10, silver 8, grey 7, blue 5).
#
# Speed 220 km/h; comfort 125/518 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 2003-2010 with a road tail to about 2022.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/porsche-cayenne.blend. References:
# citycars/references/porsche-cayenne/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.
#
# Gate C, 2026-11-16: accepted as built, no correction round authorised. Four
# recorded deviations from the photographs: the glazing band is 0.49 m deep where
# the reference car's is nearer 0.40 m, which lowers the beltline and gives an
# estate-like side; the headlamps are angular wedges rather than teardrop ovals;
# the front intake is a barred rectangular slab rather than a rounded opening; and
# the rear is a flat slab with rectangular lamps rather than a rounded tailgate
# with wrapping lamps.

